more_clear_headers 'Server' with nothing to clear does nothing (aZ, 22.11.2026 21:10:
«чтобы модуль more_clear_headers лишнюю работу не делал»). The nginx-devel of this tree
adds no "Server" line of its own (NGX_HTTP_AZ_SERVER 0,
files/patch-src_http_ngx__http__header__filter__module.c), so where the response has
none there is nothing to clear: the module does not go through the header lines for
it, nor make the empty line by which it kept nginx from adding its own. A "Server"
that is in the response (of a backend that is passed) is cleared as before. Built
against an nginx that adds the line (the macro not there, or 1), the module as it is.
Applied by post-patch in WRKSRC_headers_more, -p0.

--- src/ngx_http_headers_more_headers_out.c.orig
+++ src/ngx_http_headers_more_headers_out.c
@@ -315,6 +315,21 @@
     }
 
     if (old == NULL || *old == NULL) {
+
+#if defined(NGX_HTTP_AZ_SERVER) && !(NGX_HTTP_AZ_SERVER)
+        /*
+         * az: the nginx-devel of azsupport/ports writes no Server line of its
+         * own, so where no backend and no module has set one there is nothing
+         * to clear: no search of the header lines and no empty line made to
+         * keep nginx from adding its own
+         */
+        if (value->len == 0
+            && hv->offset == offsetof(ngx_http_headers_out_t, server))
+        {
+            return NGX_OK;
+        }
+#endif
+
         return ngx_http_set_header_helper(r, hv, value, old, 0);
     }
 
